# TypeScript incremental/composite build cache. For shared/frontend's
# composite tsconfigs this lands OUTSIDE dist/ (next to tsconfig.json, e.g.
# shared/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo) — gitignored already (*.tsbuildinfo), but NOT
# previously dockerignored. If present on the host, `COPY shared shared`
# would carry it into the image; tsc then trusts the stale cache, believes
# its (deleted-by-the-image-not-existing) dist is already up to date, and
# emits NOTHING — the exact root cause of "Cannot find module '@dpdp/shared'"
# during `docker compose build backend`. Must never enter a build context.
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
**/*.log
# Playwright output from the scripts/*.spec.mjs runs.
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
# Secrets. The root patterns alone only matched the REPO ROOT — nested files
# such as installer/config/.env were still sent into every build context. No
# Dockerfile copies them, but nothing should be one COPY away from a secret.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.production.example
*.pem
*.key
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# Not used by any image, and large: the full-stack installer's own build
# output (~1.7 GB of image tarballs and an Electron runtime), the Windows
# Gateway installer's staging/output, the desktop and Gateway Setup apps, and
# local databases/state. Excluding them is what keeps `docker build` from
# uploading gigabytes to the daemon before it starts.
installer/dist
installer/config
gateway-installer/build
gateway-installer/dist
gateway-app/dist
desktop
docs
deploy
.localdb
backend/var
scripts/.seed-demo-state.json
# A stray directory created on this machine by a mis-quoted shell command; it
# holds a .env. Never part of the product.
$generatedMfaKey*
